who is cad bane how does his origin tied  to the original star wars trilogy and is  he really just a boba fett clone keep  watching for the untold truth of the  galaxy's most terrifying bounty hunter  today it's hard to imagine the era of  clone wars dominated star wars media  without thinking of cadbane arguably one  of the most famous characters created  for that original series initially  though cadbane wasn't supposed to be  part of the show at all in fact the  original landscape for the clone wars  had no room for third party players like  bounty hunters instead the focus of the  show's stories would exclusively remain  on republic and separatist forces as  production on the show progressed  however these plans changed bounty  hunters gradually began to be  incorporated into the show's story  though even by that point cab bane's  introduction was no sure thing on the  contrary his role in the clone wars was  to be filled by pre-existing characters  from star wars law such as dutch  [Music]  however once george lucas suggested  taking the character in a visual  approach more inspired by westerns a  more original idea emerged from the  ashes of these inaugural concepts came  carbane  the distinctive look of the aliens in  the star wars galaxy is one of the best  parts of this franchise honing down the  finer intricacies of the appearances of  these creatures is a difficult task  however and inspiration for an alien  design can strike from anywhere in the  case of cadbane the clone wars crew  found his look in the distant past  specifically his design came from a  piece of unused concept art for an alien  character in the original star wars  trilogy one with guns and holsters and a  gigantic rimmed hat the artist could  never have imagined it decades earlier  but this figure was exactly what the  clone wars team was looking for when it  came to cadbane clone wars producer dave  filoni has since explained that although  this may sound like an unlikely scenario  it's a common practice for star wars  media george lucas and other artists  would often come up with character names  or alien designs in the 1970s and  promptly abandon them only for them to  find the perfect home for them decades  down the road when you're a franchise  like star wars that spans for years and  years you never know when an idea might  get a second lease on life cad bane  engages in a lot of behavior that's  pretty harsh by the standards of  villains on animated kids tv shows in  his first appearance on the clone wars  he kills a galactic senator by shooting  them in the back while a subsequent  appearance depicts him torturing a jedi  for important information whenever bane  shows up he's bound to engage in  ruthless violence which is exactly why  this particular bounty hunter has  secured such a formidable reputation  among fans of the franchise however one  play spain couldn't cross the line was  smoking on one of the bonus features on  the box set for the fourth season of the  clone wars dave filoni comments that  bane's trademark toothpick was  originally supposed to be a cigarette  this would have aligned with the western  and noir inspirations for the character  as these two genres are known for  featuring characters who aren't afraid  to light one up every now and then the  difference was of course i've been  featured on an animated kids show rather  than say casablanca  is looking at you kid  so the cigarettes were ditched and bame  was forced to satisfy his penchant for  unruly behavior in other more vicious  ways  star wars the clone wars ground to a  halt in the spring of 2013 just a few  months after disney purchased lucasfilm  a sudden developments that left multiple  seasons worth of stories on the back  burner even after two bursts of clone  wars episodes were released across 2014  and 2020 much of the show's content  remained unreleased this is a fate that  befell a proposed storyline that would  have seen cad bane returning this time  as a mentor to a young boba fett though  bane was a central figure in these  episodes this arc was primarily a boba  fett origin story right down to him  getting his iconic mandalorian armor the  latter development was supposed to occur  during a shootout between bane and fett  which would have capped off the duo's  journey from student and master to  straight-up enemies made for the season  five development cycle of the clone wars  it's unknown why this storyline wasn't  finished and released for either of the  show's brief revivals however one reason  could be that the fed vs bane showdown  ended with bane's death it's possible  that the creative team behind the clone  wars opted to scrap this episode so that  bane could remain alive and well for  future appearances  it's hard not to see some similarities  between cadbane and boba fett and not  just because they're both bounty hunters  both are men of few words but aren't  afraid to show force when the moment's  call for it they also sport some of the  most distinctive outfits in the star  wars galaxy and are particularly well  known for their snazzy headgear however  the team behind the clone wars was  particularly conscious of bane coming  off as just a clone of a more popular  bounty hunter and did everything they  could to make him unique talking to  starwars.com directly after bane's first  appearance on the clone wars director  giancarlo volpe made sure to emphasize  that and like fett bane doesn't take  prisoners though a small distinction  this detail already suggests a world of  difference between the two bounty  hunters bane is supposed to be an even  darker version of fett and is an  important entity to have lingering  around as an adolescent fete navigates  the hate he has in his heart over the  death of his father notably bane's  ruthlessness and capacity for evil serve  to demonstrate what fett might become if  he doesn't change his ways quietly  introducing this thematic detail is one  of the many reasons that bane comes off  as more than just a boba fett  doppelganger  cadbane like so many other aspects of  the star wars mythos is heavily inspired  by classic cinema in particular  everything about the character's fashion  sense owes much to western protagonists  elsewhere one of the characters earliest  appearances introduces bane draped in  darkness and shards of light like a  character from a noir movie though  existing in a sci-fi world populated by  futuristic technology cad bane is very  much evocative of vintage pop culture so  it shouldn't come as much of a surprise  to hear that voice actor corey burton  looked to the pass for inspiration on  how to voice cadbane speaking to  starwars.com burton revealed that the  primary inspiration for the character's  vocals was the distinctive voice of  peter laurie specifically burton took  particular cues from laurie's more  subdued work on assorted luxe radio  theater programs the observant follows  in a few seconds unconsciousness  in two minutes or three minutes  death  however berta made sure to emphasize  that bane is not just a redux of lori's  voice he pointed out that both he and  the clone wars crew would use this  iconic classic movie actor as a starting  basis for the performance before taking  it in new directions  given how much talent from the clone  wars was ported over to star wars rebels  you'd assume that the former show's  recurring antagonist cadbane should have  been right in line for a guest  appearance the likelihood of that  happening seemed to increase once clone  wars fan favorite characters such as  ahsoka tano and captain rex made  appearances on the program and the  series even continued darth maul's  storyline from the clone wars if these  familiar faces could show up who's to  say cadbane couldn't unfortunately for  caribbean fans the bounty hunter was  missing from the entire run of rebels  even when other clone wars scoundrels  showed up bane was simply nowhere to be  found however eagle-eyed viewers may  have spotted the closest thing to a bane  cameo on the show in one particular  rebels episode in the form of bang  graffiti on a wall behind sabine though  just a background detail this easter egg  reminded viewers that bane is very much  alive and well in this era of star wars  even before disney bought lucasfilm star  wars tv shows were all about bringing in  familiar faces for surprise appearances  just look at how jabba the hurt factored  into the clone wars movie or the guest  appearance by greedo in a season 3  episode of the series this practice has  only become more pronounced in recent  years as luca's film attempts to  reinforce a sense of unified continuity  across all its various star wars  properties one example of this was cad  bane making a surprise appearance at the  2021 series star wars the bad batch  producer jennifer corbett explained to  skywalking through the netherlands that  having bane appear on the bad batch was  more than just providing a dose of fan  service to viewers the show had already  featured the leads facing off against  bounty hunter fenik shand and following  that formidable opponent the writers  wanted to introduce an even greater  threat for the protagonist to battle  this is where cadbane came into play as  corbett and the other bad batch  personnel felt he was one of the most  ruthless figures these characters could  go toe-to-toe with and if bringing back  this adversary reinforce a grander  fictional universe the bad batch  occupied well that was just gravy too  when cad bane reappears in the bad batch  making his first appearance in a  canonical star wars property in almost a  decade he looks a little different than  viewers might remember bane hasn't  undergone a radical transformation but  he's got a new ship and his clothes have  been tweaked a little too these weren't  incidental alterations though they were  intentional enhancements to the  character meant to take him into new  directions while also paying tribute to  unrealized storylines involving bane  from the clone wars director brad rau  explained to skywalking through  neverland for the design of cadbane we  were looking at some designs that never  got into production that were in  progress in clone wars it was a lot of  fun to sort of take them out of the  garage and tinker with it and push it  and rework it a little bit so that  campaign and his ride felt familiar and  yet a little bit more nuanced and more  detailed these differences also helped  to reinforce the passage of time between  bane's last appearance and the era of  star wars history in which the bad batch  occurs by taking this visual route the  show could tip its hat towards past star  wars television while also offering up  something new for a fan favorite  character  bringing cadbane back for the bad batch  didn't just offer an opportunity to make  fans of the bounty hunter as pleased as  punch it was also a chance to bring to  life certain story beats that the clone  wars never got to play out before its  cancellation of course given how much  time had passed between the first end of  the clone wars in 2013 and the 2021  debut of the bad batch it was clear that  the original concepts for bane's  storylines couldn't just be reused whole  cloth but they could be reinterpreted to  fit newly introduced characters in the  star wars mythos in an interview with  screen rant brad rau revealed that cad  bane's appearance and the bad batch was  steeped deeply in unused designs and  story lines from the clone wars the big  showdown between bane and new character  hunter was even based on the animation  and direction of the unused battle  between bane and boba fett from the  earlier series rao explained so it's  more of us as fans behind the scenes  wanting to pay homage to that when it  comes to this galaxy far far away no  idea is ever really gone  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more luba videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

